History
-------
The touch UI started from 33333s/u60pro-devui (MIT) and Wei REN's fork. The
current touch UI is a Rust + LVGL rewrite; the remaining code derived from
those projects was rewritten in October 2026. Versions published before
2026-10-21 stay under the MIT License they were released with.

Not published:
- third_party/lvgl/ (rs/setup-src.sh fetches LVGL v9.5.0)
- ubus_list.txt (runtime dump of a real device)
Private host names in comments and docs were replaced with placeholders.

Third-party components
----------------------
- Build-time dependencies, not included: LVGL v9.5.0 (MIT, with the small
  patch in patches/) and FreeType (FreeType License or GPLv2). A statically
  linked binary carries their code; ship their license texts with any binary
  you distribute.
- No ZTE fonts or vendor binaries are included. docs/images/ are rendered by
  the offscreen render test from made-up test data.

